WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Falcon 9 booster B1063 reaches its 36th flight today, extending the record for reusable first stages.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:13.900
This is SpaceX Daily, episode 136, senators on star shield in Ukraine, grok on x, and later

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.040
the engineering angle on first stage reuse.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.180
vandenberg's base force base sends 27 optimized starlink V2 mini satellites toward orbit

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.260
on this mission, according to Shattered.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:29.640
The flight is Starlink 1515, the window opens at 3.14pm Pacific.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.720
The first stage will try to land on the drone ship of course I still love you, in the Pacific.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.420
Those optimized satellites are a revised V2 minibus, built to pack more units per launch

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.980
while SpaceX waits on larger V3 hardware.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:49.720
Booster B1063 has already flown dozens of prior Starlink missions, taking the Block 5 first

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.140
stage.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:56.300
The current Falcon 9 booster design, through repeated max-dynamic pressure, the peak aerodynamic

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.900
load, and re-entry heating.

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:03.848
Four Democratic Senators sent SpaceX a letter asking who controls Starlink and Starsheald,

00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:08.928
the national security variant of the network, and how that control is divided with the U.S.

00:01:09.908 --> 00:01:14.228
The letter cites Elon Musk's statement that Starsheald systems are owned by the government,

00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:18.008
and that speed limits are set by the military, N.V. reports.

00:01:18.008 --> 00:01:23.908
The letter asks what technical and operational authority SpaceX still has over the underlying network.

00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:29.528
Jean Shaheen, Richard Blumenthal, Sheldon Whitehouse, and Chris Coons sign the document.

00:01:30.068 --> 00:01:33.448
Addressed to SpaceX Vice President of Legal Christopher Cardachi,

00:01:34.188 --> 00:01:40.208
the Senators note that SpaceX owns and operates the Starlink infrastructure that certain star shield services rely on.

00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:47.348
The Senators want answers on whether the company can restrict access during military operations or national security emergencies.

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:47.548
policies.

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:52.569
Grok drew a public nod from Elon Musk for its handling of technical questions.

00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:57.369
The October 20th post on X follows earlier comments on GrokBot usage.

00:01:58.169 --> 00:02:02.849
Elon Musk said in a separate X post that a rewrite of the Android app addressed longstanding

00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:04.049
performance problems.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:08.049
Musk described the prior version as really bad for such a long time.

00:02:08.689 --> 00:02:13.149
