00:04:10.332 --> 00:04:14.752
Worth keeping an eye on is Ukraine's military report that star-shield speed limits have

00:04:14.752 --> 00:04:19.172
cut drone interceptor effectiveness to roughly 54 percent of prior capability.

00:04:19.932 --> 00:04:25.412
Tech Insider says the restrictions cut service above 100 miles per hour, forcing slower flight

00:04:25.412 --> 00:04:28.392
profiles that limit response time against incoming threats.

00:04:29.012 --> 00:04:33.512
Ukrainian officials say those drops affect helicopter and drone operations against Shahed

00:04:33.512 --> 00:04:34.212
type targets.

00:04:34.212 --> 00:04:39.072
its. Resolving it would take either a US government policy change or technical adjustments

00:04:39.072 --> 00:04:45.037
to the terminal SpaceX operates under contract. Reuse physics is the engineering angle today,

00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:50.877
because a first stage only flies again if the energy budget closes. Each ascent burns roughly

00:04:50.877 --> 00:04:56.797
400 tons of propellant to reach staging velocity. The rocket equation says the velocity gain depends

00:04:56.797 --> 00:05:02.257
on how much of the vehicle is spent as exhaust. Most of that ascent load exists to accelerate

00:05:02.257 --> 00:05:07.617
the rest of the ascent load, plus the upper stage. The return dumps the gained energy in three

00:05:07.617 --> 00:05:13.337
burns, boost back to reverse, entry to survive Mach 8 and landing over the drone ship.

00:05:13.837 --> 00:05:19.837
A back of envelope check on that Mach number. Sea level speed of sound is about 340 meters per second,

00:05:20.377 --> 00:05:27.177
so it is on the order of 2.7 kilometers per second. Textbook orbital speed is about 7.8 kilometers per

00:05:27.177 --> 00:05:31.977
second, which is why the first stage is not the orbital vehicle. It never has to kill

00:05:31.977 --> 00:05:36.557
full orbital energy on the way home. It still has to kill a hypersonic chunk of it.

00:05:37.017 --> 00:05:41.637
Kinetic energy scales with the square of speed, so even a fraction of orbital velocity

00:05:41.637 --> 00:05:46.857
is not a gentle stop. The entry burn exists to cut that speed before the airframe has to

00:05:46.857 --> 00:05:52.217
eat it as heat. The structure sees peak dynamic pressure twice per mission, plus the thermal

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:58.157
pulse of that hypersonic return. Dynamic pressure is the punch of air at speed, density times

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:03.017
velocity squared over 2. The stage gets one punch going up through the thick atmosphere,

00:06:03.597 --> 00:06:08.157
and another coming back in. Thermal protection and the tank walls have to like both.

00:06:08.757 --> 00:06:13.857
Because the vehicle was sized for a single use plus margin, extra propellant for recovery is

00:06:13.857 --> 00:06:19.657
only about 30% of the ascent total. Recovery burns right on left over propellant after staging,

00:06:19.657 --> 00:06:22.537
moving, so the vehicle is not lifting a second full stack.

00:06:23.077 --> 00:06:27.457
The stage spends that margin while still carrying fluid, then re-enters lighter.

00:06:27.977 --> 00:06:32.277
That is why the recovery allocation can stay a minority of the ascent load instead of

00:06:32.277 --> 00:06:33.097
doubling the vehicle.

00:06:33.717 --> 00:06:39.637
Over many cycles, cumulative propellant cost per flight falls by a factor of roughly 30 compared

00:06:39.637 --> 00:06:41.477
with building a new stage each time.

00:06:42.097 --> 00:06:47.217
The magic wand number is the raw inputs, kerosene, liquid oxygen, and tank metal.

00:06:47.217 --> 00:06:52.977
The idiot index, how many times the finished booster costs over those raw inputs, stays

00:06:52.977 --> 00:06:56.557
high because turbo pumps and avionics dwarf the commodity bill.

00:06:57.077 --> 00:06:59.257
A turbo pump is not priced like aluminum.

00:07:00.177 --> 00:07:03.817
Avionics and turbo pumps do not get cheaper just because the stage flies again.

00:07:04.297 --> 00:07:05.317
They get amortized.

00:07:05.737 --> 00:07:10.637
The floor is the sum of propellant, a small slice of those components life, and however many

00:07:10.637 --> 00:07:12.577
technician hours the pad still demands.

00:07:12.577 --> 00:07:17.937
hands. If inspection, refurbishment, and launch site overhead drop below 10% of original

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:23.757
build cost, per-flight economics approach that raw material and avionics floor. If the

00:07:23.757 --> 00:07:28.737
hours come down, the idiot index of a flown stage collapses toward the magic wand number.

00:07:29.357 --> 00:07:34.157
Leave the hours high and it is an expendable rocket that happens to land. Ground operations

00:07:34.157 --> 00:07:39.197
now set the next limit, not the physics of the burns. Orbital class first stages stay

00:07:39.197 --> 00:07:42.837
harder to reuse than suborbital hoppers for the same energy reason.

00:07:43.317 --> 00:07:47.837
A student-scale hopper like Calibri only needs a low-speed vertical landing at roughly

00:07:47.837 --> 00:07:51.857
1.2 kN of thrust and 100 kG of mass.

00:07:52.357 --> 00:07:57.617
It never sees hypersonic heating, multi-engine throttling after 100-plus kilometer trajectory,

00:07:58.117 --> 00:08:01.357
or a boost back while still carrying residual upper-stage mass.

00:08:01.977 --> 00:08:07.057
Those loads scale with the square velocity and the cube of linear dimensions, so a clean

00:08:07.057 --> 00:08:10.137
marine hopper landing does not become operational orbital reuse.

00:08:10.757 --> 00:08:15.517
A back-of-end-valote figure on the Q-Blaw, stretch of vehicle three times longer in every

00:08:15.517 --> 00:08:20.297
dimension and the mass to keep intact is on the order of 27 times, not three.

00:08:20.957 --> 00:08:25.817
Velocity squared on the heat and arrow-side stacks on top of that, which is the gap between

00:08:25.817 --> 00:08:27.417
a hopper and an orbital booster.

00:08:28.077 --> 00:08:33.097
A hopper at that mass never pays the heat tax, so its idiot index is mostly structure

00:08:33.097 --> 00:08:36.817
and avionics, not thermal protection and engine out throttle profiles.

00:08:37.417 --> 00:08:39.357
None of that is a reason reuse fails.

00:08:39.837 --> 00:08:44.137
It is why the recovery propellant margin and a conservative tank set had to be in the

00:08:44.137 --> 00:08:46.577
original design, not bolted on later.

00:08:47.197 --> 00:08:52.537
Falcon 9 absorbs the orbital loads by carrying extra propellant margin and flying the same structural

00:08:52.537 --> 00:08:55.177
tank set through repeated thermal and pressure cycles.

00:08:55.757 --> 00:09:00.197
Each extra flight checks that the original factor of safety assumption still hold after

00:09:00.197 --> 00:09:01.817
another full envelope exposure.

00:09:01.817 --> 00:09:07.697
Super Heavy, Starship's first stage lives under that same accounting, and comparable flight

00:09:07.697 --> 00:09:12.237
counts would make rapid reuse the dominant advantage over expendable architectures.

00:09:12.697 --> 00:09:14.397
The remaining question is process.

00:09:15.017 --> 00:09:19.377
Whether inspection hours and fatigue allow that floor to be reached, or whether tear-down

00:09:19.377 --> 00:09:20.577
rules get there first.

00:09:21.177 --> 00:09:25.857
On the public tape, SPCX slipped roughly half a percent versus the prior close.

